th a basic  intro into handling payments then you  could branch off to strong customer  authentication or stripe connect or some  other advanced concept this would allow  me to roll out content more quickly in a  modular format and it'll make the  content easier for you to consume  because you won't have to go through  things that you don't care about now a  few months ago I started working on a  project called spelt fire it's just a  simple open source library that  integrates firebase into some small  components but the main reason I built  it in the first place is because I want  to roll out several advanced UI  components for firebase users that can  be dropped into any framework like  imagine a file uploader widget that can  be dropped into your friend  that automatically integrates with your  back-end infrastructure or an email pass  trought education form that integrates  with any design system now that's  obviously a very big project that takes  a lot of work to do right so I don't  want to rush anything out the door the  last thing I want to talk about is the  migration of angular firebase into fire  ship IO  all of the full courses have been  migrated over already but there's still  a lot of individual lessons on angular  firebase that need to be migrated that  process will be 100% complete by January  1st and the angular firebase site will  redirect a fire ship  none of that content is going away it's  just being fully integrated under one  roof and you can access it with the  angular tag on fire ship at any time I  think that's all the updates I have  right now thanks again for all of these  supports and I will see you again in  2020 oh wait I almost forgot we still  have another t-shirt to give away  Congrats Locke Sean Pereira you are the  second t-shirt winner of the video  thanks again everybody I will talk to  you soon
 

